# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — keep the kaniko/CI build context small.
#
# Why this exists: `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile ships the whole repo into
# kaniko, which holds each layer's tar in memory. Without this file the context
# was ~860 MB — 824 MB of it under .beads/ (agent dispatch traces that are
# tracked into git). The server-image build OOMKilled (exit 137) on the iad-ci
# nodes (~6.2 Gi allocatable) even though its cgroup limit is 8 Gi: the node
# physically cannot back that much, so kaniko was killed by node-pressure.
# That produced a "ghost tag": VERSION bumped on main (by resolve-version) but
# no image actually published, so any fleet bump to it ImagePullBackOff'd.
# See bead bf-3u9pv0 and the historical 0.1.467 ghost-tag incident.
#
# The runtime images are `FROM scratch` containing only compiled Go binaries.
# There are NO //go:embed directives in the tree, so the build needs exactly
# the Go source (go.mod/go.sum + cmd/ internal/ tests/) and nothing else.
# Excluding every non-source path below is therefore safe.
# =============================================================================

# VCS + bead/agent tooling — 824 MB of traces/db/backups, the dominant cost.
.git/
.gitignore
.beads/
.claude/
.needle.yaml
.needle-predispatch-sha
.needle-*

# Stale committed build OUTPUTS — the Dockerfile rebuilds these from source.
armor
armor-decrypt
restore-verifier
*.test
target/

# Docs / notes / scratch / planning — not in the runtime image.
docs/
notes/
scratch/
*.md

# Deployment manifests / scripts / samples / drift config — runtime needs none.
k8s/
deploy/
# Keep the shared Docker/CI release gate while excluding every other helper.
scripts/*
!scripts/release-gate.sh
samples/
config/
armor_deployments.json

# Local editor / OS cruft.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
